Non-zero mutually orthogonal vectors are linearly independent. If $sum_i alpha_i vb(v_i) = vb(0)$, taking the inner product with $vb(v_j)$ gives
$ 0 = iprod(vb(v_j), sum_i alpha_i vb(v_i)) = alpha_j iprod(vb(v_j), vb(v_j)), $
so $alpha_j abs(vb(v_j))^2 = 0$ forces $alpha_j = 0$ by positive definiteness, for every $j$.
